{"title":"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider infinite sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5dd8e5b43242c6153db18b4123a70c811990b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> of positive reals such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78cc2ebaf7b90d027f60713856ec8e83e3581b57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba0362ff7851289a81246661b9b4e4b8f76d56e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0\\ge x_1\\ge x_2\\ge\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>a) Prove that for every such sequence there is an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340797a8fa9f1a06b10ce9e764998830b15ca755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> such that:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/33618b7c852ba18eeed45d1d7cfcbf27d6c1d469.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{x_0^2\\over x_1}+{x_1^2\\over x_2}+\\ldots+{x_{n-1}^2\\over x_n}\\ge3.999.\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>b) Find such a sequence such that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83d451858c798ddc4e67ff59cd9613d41a1fd428.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{x_0^2\\over x_1}+{x_1^2\\over x_2}+\\ldots+{x_{n-1}^2\\over x_n}&lt;4.\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"42\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Cauchy, the LHS is at least:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d634c4d5a5d40452717e9a71290cd611f08eaca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(x_{0}+...+x_{n-1})^{2}}{x_{1}+...+x_{n}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"143\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>It is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/3422025bb96059db79f2ccd262bed2e62df0de01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3cae9e87de32f5d14a31fc404340f42bc6567ace.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n}\\le \\frac{x_{1}+...+x_{n-1}}{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"159\" height=\"36\" />\n</p><p>We thus have that the LHS is at least:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acfe6cb63a7e58654613e786b350cf711f4c7383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{1+2(x_{1}+...+x_{n-1})+(x_{1}+...+x_{n-1})^{2}}{x_{1}+...+x_{n-1}})(\\frac{n-1}{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"406\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Applying 2-variable AM-GM to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/0/9605237671a546a503a64b4b1e39b4d425d7030d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_{1}+...+x_{n-1})^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"19\" /> the LHS is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c98c085a415eb5c9b38d4b0bd86abd8ed54869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(\\frac{n-1}{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>We then simply choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e9a276fd310834e65b8e477cb6e2e8502fd3cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(\\frac{n-1}{n}) \\ge 3.999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"134\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Part b) is likely to occur only if both the AM-GM and Cauchy equality conditions are close to met, or if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/894acb358a3c97e6ea693e59b9f6825d988b737f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1=x_{1}+x_{2}+...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734b6daa3a109cffbcbe14ee03dc8065d404579a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_{0}}{x_{1}}=\\frac{x_{1}}{x_{2}}=...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"105\" height=\"35\" />, respectively. This points to the geometric series with common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> as the equality case.\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by n^4 4. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p722917\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>b) is immediate by taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/d/c2de0d03d71c836e9a301fd6dd02e6b6ee2e6edc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = 2^{-i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>For a), we prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b63b5b17ab85f158ad8b492898c235e098cce72f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LHS \\ge 2^{2^0 + 2^{-1}+...+ 2^{2-n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"180\" height=\"21\" />, and taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/694a761d1744afe15db60a60ee38458b687488d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\to \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"10\" /> will yield the result. (Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> gives the empty sum, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a9701b6b3ed3f28c1eb04eb9387b16f9c05c463b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LHS \\ge 2^0=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"117\" height=\"19\" />, which is trivial).\n</p><p>The proof is not hard. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3b63c17213f84d730e0de1f8c08597f7a648e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> terms, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/18340892dadb937ba2e045f386a73f64d2fb1a3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_n = s_{n-2} + \\dfrac{x_{n-2}^2}{x_{n-1}} + \\dfrac{x_{n-1}^2}{x_n} \\ge s_{n-2} + 2^{2^0} x_{n-2} \\sqrt{\\dfrac{x_{n-1}}{x_n}} \\ge s_{n-2} + 2^{2^0} x_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"539\" height=\"44\" />. This in turn is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f2cb70e0d2299c9c1ffa2c611da341dd78ba599.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{n-3} + \\dfrac{x_{n-3}^2}{x_{n-2}} + 2^{2^0} x_{n-2}\\ge s_{n-3} + 2^{2^0 +  2^{-1}} x_{n-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"350\" height=\"42\" />. By repeatedly applying AM-GM to the last two terms of the sum, collecting powers of two, and cancelling variables, we eventually obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/71051fe07baf86652dd84f03529e50d85fd1fd7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_0 + \\dfrac{x_0^2}{x_1} + 2^{2^0 + 2^1 + ... + 2^{3-n}}x_1 \\ge 0 + 2^{2^0 + 2^1 + ... + 2^{2-n}}x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"388\" height=\"41\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by tastymath75025. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p10580878\">[2]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO\" title=\"1982 IMO\">1982 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017121332\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 160/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 895/2097152 bytes\